    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Env-fingerprint derivation: SHA256(COMPUTERNAME+USERDOMAIN)", "technique": "T1480.001", "what_happened": "At 2032-10-11 16:18:08 UTC, AMSI EID 4104 captures PowerShell scriptblock that concatenates $env:COMPUTERNAME and $env:USERDOMAIN, then computes [System.Security.Cryptography.SHA256]::Create().ComputeHash(...) to produce a 32-byte fingerprint hex-encoded. Rule 92210 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Using SHA256(env vars) as KEY MATERIAL is the canonical 'environment-keyed' decryption primitive — the malware cannot decrypt its payload unless it runs on the exact target machine."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Comparison against hardcoded target fingerprint", "technique": "T1480.001", "what_happened": "At 2032-10-11 16:18:11, AMSI scriptblock includes literal '$targetFingerprint = 3d7b2e1a9f4c5d6e8b0a1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f' and gate '$fpHex -eq $targetFingerprint'. Rule 92200 triggered.", "chain_reason": "Hardcoded target fingerprint = the malware author knows EXACTLY which machine it should run on. This is a stronger guardrail than PB096 t01's allowlist-style match: a hash collision is effectively impossible, so payload decryption is mathematically gated."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "AES-CBC decryptor instantiated with env-derived key + zero IV", "technique": "T1480.001", "what_happened": "At 2032-10-11 16:18:14, AMSI scriptblock instantiates [System.Security.Cryptography.Aes]::Create() with Mode=CBC, Padding=PKCS7, Key=fingerprint(32 bytes), IV=[byte[]](0x00 * 16), then calls CreateDecryptor().TransformFinalBlock(...) on an embedded base64 blob.", "chain_reason": "AES-256-CBC with a key derived from environment vars is the exact Conti / LockBit loader pattern. The decryption is mathematically guaranteed to fail unless the host matches the target fingerprint."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Proof file written documenting guardrail outcome", "technique": "T1480.001", "what_happened": "At 2032-10-11 16:18:18, Sysmon EID 11 reports creation of C:\\Users\\r.morrison\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\p96_t02_proof_161808.txt. Content depends on gate outcome: 'ENV_KEYED_GUARDRAIL_HIT fingerprint=<hex> ts=<...>' if mismatch, OR the decrypted payload string if match.", "chain_reason": "The proof file documents whether the gate was crossed. Reading its content tells us whether this host matched the target fingerprint or not — which is decisive for severity."}
